---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AUTHOR, CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../consts";
---

<Base title="Terms" description="The terms for reading Teximos and using its pages and feed.">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="kicker">Terms</span>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>

      <div class="prose column">
        <p>
          These terms apply to teximos.com and its feed. By reading the site or
          using it, you agree to them. They were last updated on {LEGAL_UPDATED}.
        </p>

        <h2>What Teximos is</h2>
        <p>
          Teximos is an independent publication about technology. It reports on
          and explains news, releases, research and policy, and it gives opinion
          where a piece says it is opinion. Nothing on the site is legal, security,
          financial, medical or other professional advice. Before you act on
          anything you read here, check it against the primary source and take
          your own advice.
        </p>

        <h2>Ownership of the text</h2>
        <p>
          The written pieces on Teximos are copyright {AUTHOR.name}. You may quote
          a passage with a credit and a link back to the piece. You may not
          republish a whole piece, or make it available for others to copy,
          without written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>Images and third party material</h2>
        <p>
          Images, quotations and figures belong to their owners. Where a piece
          uses material that is in the public domain, from a Creative Commons
          licence or from another source, the piece credits it. Those credits
          are part of the licence and must be kept if you reuse the image.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Each piece is written from primary sources where they could be reached,
          and the piece says where they could not. The site is provided as it is,
          and mistakes happen. If something is wrong, write to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Corrections are
          made in place and the change is noted.
        </p>

        <h2>Links</h2>
        <p>
          Teximos links to other sites for reference. We do not control those
          sites and are not responsible for their content. A link is not an
          endorsement.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site and its feed are provided without warranty of any kind, express
          or implied. We do not promise that the site will always be available,
          error free or suitable for any particular purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>Limit of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent the law allows, Teximos and its author are not
          liable for any loss or damage arising from reading the site or relying on
          what it says.
        </p>

        <h2>Takedown and legal notices</h2>
        <p>
          If you own material on the site and believe it is used wrongly, or if
          you have a legal notice to send, write to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Include the
          address of the page and enough detail for us to find the material. We
          will respond and act in good faith.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms can change. When they do, the date at the top changes too,
          and the new terms apply from that date.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, USA,
          without regard to its conflict of laws rules. Disputes are to be brought
          in the courts of California.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
</content>
